    "---\nname: ym-freeze-clay-target\ndescription: Freeze the exact pure Yang--Mills existence and mass-gap target, axiomatic endpoint, quantifiers, theory identity, and claim level. Use before designing a proof, reviewing a claimed solution, comparing regulators, or when mass gap, confinement, lattice gaps, or continuum existence risk being conflated.\n---\n\n## Abducer Integration Guards\n\n- Activate this skill only for `yang-mills-existence-and-mass-gap-target` or an explicitly marked Yang-Mills calibration task.\n- Treat imported representational-dynamics artifacts as restricted, finite, conditional, or support evidence unless a later proof discharges their frontier hypotheses.\n- Emit claim level, non-claims, hard gate, hypotheses, falsifier, and demotion trigger before any promotion.\n- Compose with the target-neutral proof-depth skills: pressure formalization, hard-gate selection, nontriviality audit, anti-definitionality audit, same-domain transfer certification, and declarative learning extraction.\n- State efficient representation requirements: preserved observables, morphisms or recovery maps, invariants, error budgets, equivalence policy, locality or cutoff budget, transfer interface, and falsifiers.\n- Do not let a transfer theorem pass if the target property is built into the bridge definition; require independently stated source and target objects plus a consequence delta.\n- Preserve the four-cycle, recursion-depth-one publication-consolidation limit for local subgoals.\n- Source provenance: `agentic/external/yang_mills_representational_dynamics/2026-07-20/skill_bundle/11_vscode_codex_skill_bundle/.agents/skills/ym-freeze-clay-target/SKILL.md`.\n\n## Mathematical Invariants\n\nPreserve the Yang--Mills mathematical object: compact simple gauge group, pure gauge content, gauge-invariant observable algebra, regulator/cutoff/volume/coupling regime, reflection positivity, locality, OS reconstruction route, continuum limit order, and Hamiltonian spectral target. Any representation, morphism, RG step, or restricted model must state which invariants are preserved, which error budgets are allowed, and which edge case or counterexample would break transfer.\n\n## Epistemic Discipline\n\nEvery output must state epistemic status, claim level, evidence citation, source artifacts, explicit unknowns, and validation handoff. Treat physical relevance, literature-gap warrant, and frontier comparison as hard gates; unsupported implications stay conditional, blocked, or `requires_prior_art`.\n\n## Failure/Demotion\n\nDemote or quarantine if the skill assumes a mass gap, clustering, confinement, continuum existence, regulator independence, positivity, locality, observable density, or theory identity instead of proving it. Disconfirming evidence, prior-art collision, target-equivalent bridge definitions, or missing counterexample tests block promotion to a major YM publication pathway.\n\n# Freeze the Yang--Mills Target\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. State the theory: compact simple gauge group, pure gauge content, four-dimensional Euclidean/Minkowski spacetime, and excluded extensions.\n2. State the axiomatic endpoint and the reconstruction route.\n3. State the spectral target, including vacuum sector, positivity, finiteness, and nontriviality.\n4. Separate mass gap, exponential clustering, confinement, area law, and isolated-particle claims.\n5. Partition all statements into premises, definitions, intermediate obligations, targets, and evidence.\n6. Assign the strongest permissible claim level:\n   - C0 conceptual;\n   - C1 formal calculus;\n   - C2 abstract transfer theorem;\n   - C3 restricted model;\n   - C4 regulated four-dimensional theorem;\n   - C5 continuum-stable theorem;\n   - C6 full Clay conclusion.\n7. Emit a claim ledger and a list of forbidden inferences.\n\n## Required checks\n\n- Reject any formulation that assumes clustering, a positive correlation length, or an infrared massive basin without proving it.\n- Mark strong-coupling lattice results as regulated or infinite-lattice results, not continuum Yang--Mills.\n- Require both a nontrivial axiomatic theory and a Hamiltonian spectral gap for C6.\n- Keep matter, supersymmetry, Higgs fields, large-N limits, and altered dimensions outside the target unless explicitly labeled as calibration models.\n- Record every regulator, volume, cutoff, and coupling quantifier.\n\n## Output contract\n\nReturn: frozen theorem statement; scope table; claim level; premise/target partition; unresolved obligations; and falsification conditions. Stop if the theory cannot be identified without assuming the target property.\n\n## Packaged PRISM Output Contract\n\nReturn exactly the generated `DomainScopeGrounding` JSON object. Do not paraphrase closed variant values.\n\n- Follow the exact generated JSON schema without extra fields.\n",
